0. Additional Use Grant (plain language, binding)

(a) Individuals. If you are a natural person, you may use the Licensed Work
    free of charge for:
      - personal security research and education;
      - participation in bug bounty programs, vulnerability disclosure
        programs, and capture-the-flag exercises — including professional
        participation for which you receive monetary rewards;
      - automation of your own workflows on systems you own or are
        authorized in writing to test.

(b) Legal entities. If you are a company, organization, or institution, you
    may use the Licensed Work free of charge only for:
      - internal security research on systems you own or are authorized in
        writing to test;
      - coordinated vulnerability disclosure and authorized testing that
        you do not resell or productize.

(c) Commercial use — requiring a paid license — includes, without
    limitation:
      - embedding or bundling the Licensed Work (or a derivative of it) in
        any product, service, platform, or offering made available to third
        parties, whether free or paid;
      - providing automated testing, scanning, or browser-automation
        capabilities as a service to third parties, regardless of whether
        the activity could otherwise be described as security research or
        bug bounty work;
      - operating the Licensed Work for the benefit of clients, customers,
        or employers as part of a paid engagement, by anyone other than a
        natural person acting individually under (a);
      - redistributing the Licensed Work as part of a commercial offering.

    Anti-loophole clause: describing any of the activities in (c) as "bug
    bounty work", "security research", or "authorized testing" does not
    bring them within the free grant. The free grant follows the user and
    the offering, not the label of the activity.

(d) Contributions. Pull requests and patches you submit to the Licensor are
    licensed to the Licensor under the same terms as this license, so the
    project can accept and redistribute them.

